[1] blocks = h + total depth; core - c = sum of depths over the valleys above each column; core area - area = sum of depth x span; no two valleys cross; at most w - 2 valleys, none iff unimodal; horizontally visible pairs = (w - 1) + valleys; all castles w <= 9, h <= 5: True
[2] the stack scan agrees with brute force (valleys and block parity), w <= 9, h <= 5: True
[3] shape lemma: exactly one valley iff exactly one wall pair has a flat floor below both walls, unimodal sides, and (c_i >= c_j, right side weakly decreasing) or (c_i <= c_j, left side weakly increasing); w <= 9, h <= 5: True
[4] valley castles = (h - 1)^2 C(w + 2h - 3, 2h), 1 <= w <= 16, 1 <= h <= 7: True
[5] case (A) gives C(w + 2h - 3, 2h) for each 1 <= f < c_j <= h, and its castles with c_j = h are the overlap, (h - 1) C(w + 2h - 3, 2h); w <= 9, h <= 5: True
[6] depth d: (2h - 1 - 2d) C(w + 2h - 3, 2h); even-block C(h, 2) or C(h - 1, 2) times C(w + 2h - 3, 2h) as h is odd or even, odd-block the other; w <= 9, h <= 5: True
[6] parity split and S_valley = (-1)^(h+1) (h - 1) C(w + 2h - 3, 2h) by the scan, w <= 16, h <= 7: True
